# Normalize line endings in the repository to LF for every text file.
#
# This exists because CI has a byte-identity guard: baseline-comparison.yml
# regenerates artifacts/triton_ptx_vectorization.json and runs
# `git diff --exit-code` against the committed copy. Without this file that
# guard's verdict depends on each developer's core.autocrlf setting -- a
# contributor with autocrlf=false on Windows would commit CRLF and the diff
# would fail on content that is semantically identical. Pinning eol here makes
# it a property of the repository instead of a property of a workstation.
#
# The generating code pins LF at the point of write as well (newline="\n" in
# scripts/triton_codegen_check.py and the kernelforge writers), so the two
# layers agree: the file is written as LF and stored as LF.
* text eol=lf

# Nsight Compute captures are a binary profiler format. Git's auto-detection
# already classifies this one correctly, but state it so a future capture that
# happens to look text-like early on is never mangled by eol conversion.
*.ncu-rep binary
